    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d860">

                <pb facs="0994" n="882" xml:id="pg882"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.113 (Manchuria) Petroleum/82: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-15T14:00:00-05:00">February 15, 1935—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>20. Your 31, February 15, 11 a.m. The Department perceives no objection to joint
                    informal oral representations and approves the suggestion contained in the
                    penultimate sentence of your telegram.<anchor n="78" xml:id="d860-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d860-f1" n="78" xml:id="d860-f1-content">
                <p>The Ambassador in Japan reported in telegram No. 34, February 19, 6 p.m., that
                    joint oral representations were made that day and were received favorably
                    (693.113 (Manchuria) Petroleum/83).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
